# Image versions the stack runs, committed so that `git pull` alone brings a
# deployment up to date. Renovate bumps them here, and the Makefile reads this
# file before .env, so a `git pull` and `make update` (docs/MAKE_COMMANDS.md)
# are all an existing deployment needs to follow main.
#
# Not a copy to edit. .env holds the deployment's own settings and no
# versions, so a pin put back into .env overrides the one here for as long as
# it stays there: that is how a deliberate hold works. Mark it with a comment
# line starting `# hold` directly above it, saying why, so that
# `make migrate_versions` (which `make update` runs) keeps it rather than
# clearing it as a stale copy:
#
#   # hold: Jellyfin 10.11 runs a one way database migration
#   JELLYFIN_VERSION=10.10.7
#
# The Makefile exports every variable named here, so compose, which takes the
# environment over .env, sees the value make resolved. A compose command run
# by hand needs the same, see docs/MAKE_COMMANDS.md, "Image versions".
#
# Lines without a # renovate: annotation use floating/channel tags managed manually.
# tests/test_renovate_pins.py enforces that: a pin added here with no annotation
# and no digest fails the suite rather than quietly going unwatched.
# renovate: depName=docker.io/linuxserver/bazarr
